Note: `address` and `city` have `@NotNull`/`@Size(min=1)` but **no `@Pattern`**, which is exactly why the controller's `validateRequiredFields` exists — a whitespace-only value passes `@Size(min=1)` but is caught by the `isBlank()` check. Also note the DTO `telephone` pattern (`^[0-9]*$`, max 20) is *looser* than the entity's telephone constraint (§3 below: exactly 10 digits).

### 5. `@Valid` usage / validators / lifecycle callbacks

- `@Valid` on the request body: `OwnersApi.java:86`; interface `@Validated` at `:44`.
- Custom validator: `validateRequiredFields`/`requireText` (shown in §2).
- Custom exception: `src/main/java/.../rest/controller/RequiredFieldsMissingException.java` (whole file, 25-37) — a `RuntimeException` carrying the field list.
- **No** `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@PreUpdate`/entity listeners anywhere. The Owner/Person/BaseEntity entities have only JPA mapping + Bean Validation annotations, no lifecycle callbacks.
- The only other project validator is `PetAgeValidator` (pet path only) — not on the owner creation path.

### 3b. Owner entity + its Bean Validation annotations

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java:35-53`:

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "owners")
public class Owner extends Person {
    @Column(name = "address")
    @NotEmpty
    private String address;

    @Column(name = "city")
    @NotEmpty
    private String city;

    @Column(name = "telephone")
    @NotEmpty
    @Digits(fraction = 0, integer = 10)
    @Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{10}$", message = "Phone number must be exactly 10 digits")
    private String telephone;

    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<Pet> pets;
```

Inherited fields — `src/main/java/.../model/Person.java:29-37`:

```java
@MappedSuperclass
public class Person extends BaseEntity {
    @Column(name = "first_name")
    @NotEmpty
    protected String firstName;

    @Column(name = "last_name")
    @NotEmpty
    protected String lastName;
```

Id — `src/main/java/.../model/BaseEntity.java:31-47`: `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY) protected Integer id;` plus `isNew()` returning `id == null`.

Important: these entity-level constraints (`@NotEmpty`, `@Digits`, exact-10-digit `@Pattern`) are declared on the entity, but on this path validation is driven by the DTO (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`), and the entity is written via Spring Data `save` — Hibernate bean validation on flush (`javax.persistence.validation`) would apply the entity constraints at persist time if enabled (default `AUTO`). This is the one place where the stricter entity telephone rule (`^[0-9]{10}$`) could reject a value the DTO accepted.

### 6. Service + repository save logic (no custom save)

Service interface method implemented in `src/main/java/.../service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:232-237`:

```java
    @Override
    @Transactional
    public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);

    }
```

`@Transactional` (Spring) opens the transaction here. The active `ownerRepository` is `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (`src/main/java/.../repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`), which extends `OwnerRepository` and `Repository<Owner, Integer>`. `save` is **not customized** — it is Spring Data JPA's default `SimpleJpaRepository.save` (persist when `isNew()`, i.e. id null; merge otherwise). Only the finder queries are overridden with `@Query`. There is no JDBC/JPA hand-written impl active (those exist under `repository/jdbc` and `repository/jpa` but are gated to other profiles).

### 7. Interceptors / event listeners / side effects

- **No** `ApplicationEventPublisher`, no application events, no `@EventListener`, no auditing.
- `CallMonitoringAspect` (`src/main/java/.../util/CallMonitoringAspect.java:77`) advises `within(@org.springframework.stereotype.Repository *)`. Spring Data JPA repositories are **not** annotated `@Repository`, so — as the class Javadoc itself states ("Spring-data-jpa doesn't have any correctly annotated classes to join on") — this aspect does **not** fire on the owner-creation path under the active `spring-data-jpa` profile.
- Error handling for the path is centralized in `src/main/java/.../rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`: `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 (`:134`), `RequiredFieldsMissingException` → 400 (`:181`), `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404 (`:114`), `AccessDeniedException` re-thrown for Security (`:85`), catch-all → 500 (`:97`).

### Summary of the effective ordering
`@PreAuthorize` role check → `@Valid` DTO Bean Validation (`OwnerFieldsDto` getters) → controller `validateRequiredFields` blank check → MapStruct map → `@Transactional saveOwner` → `SpringDataOwnerRepository.save` (default persist) → Hibernate flush (entity-level constraints may apply) → `201 CREATED` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. No lifecycle callbacks, events, or custom repository code participate.
